cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "scint-fibre-fastsim: scintillator and wavelength-shifting fibre optical Monte Carlo for fast detector simulation"
version: "0.1.6"
date-released: "2026-11-20"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24418804"
authors:
  - family-names: Mina
    given-names: Rob
    affiliation: "University of Virginia"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2241-8566"
repository-code: "https://github.com/RobMina/scint-fibre-fastsim"
license: "Apache-2.0"
abstract: >-
  scint-fibre-fastsim simulates scintillation light in extruded scintillator strips read out by wavelength-shifting fibres, on JAX devices (CPU or GPU, float32 or float64), and generates the optical lookup tables that fast detector simulations draw from. One experiment-neutral optical core (a JAX port of the table mode of the public CRVStandalone Geant4 optical simulation) serves parametric geometry families and a common photosensor interface with SiPM and APD backends; a toy self-check and declared Geant4 compare plans come with it.
keywords:
  - "fast simulation"
  - "scintillator"
  - "wavelength-shifting fibre"
  - "optical photons"
  - "lookup tables"
  - "JAX"
  - "particle physics"
references:
  - type: "software"
    title: "CRVStandalone"
    authors:
      - name: "Mu2e Collaboration"
    repository-code: "https://github.com/Mu2e/CRVStandalone"
    license: "Apache-2.0"
